{
  "info": {
    "name": "Doctor Tracker API",
    "description": "REST API for Doctor Tracker (Express + MongoDB).\n\n**Quick start**\n1. Start the API (`npm run dev`) and seed data (`npm run seed:fresh`).\n2. Run **Auth → Login** — the access token is saved to `{{token}}` (used by every request via collection-level Bearer auth) and the refresh token to `{{refreshToken}}`.\n   When the access token expires (15 min) you get `401` with `code: \"TOKEN_EXPIRED\"` — run **Auth → Refresh token**.\n3. Run **Doctors → Create doctor**, then **Patients → Create patient** — their ids are saved to `{{doctorId}}` / `{{patientId}}`, so the other requests work without copy-pasting.\n\nOr open the collection and click **Run** to execute everything in order.\n\nResponses: `{ success, data, meta? }` on success, `{ success: false, message, errors? }` on error.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5000/api"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@doctortracker.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "Admin@12345"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Access token (saved by Login / Refresh)"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Refresh token (saved by Login / Refresh)"
    },
    {
      "key": "doctorId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "patientId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health check",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Public. 200 when the database is connected, 503 otherwise."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', res.data.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', res.data.refreshToken);",
                  "pm.test('Both tokens returned', () => { pm.expect(res.data.accessToken).to.be.a('string'); pm.expect(res.data.refreshToken).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns `{ user, accessToken, accessTokenExpiresAt, refreshToken, refreshTokenExpiresAt }` and sets two httpOnly cookies (access on `/`, refresh on `/api/auth` only).\n\nThe test script saves `{{token}}` (access, 15 min) and `{{refreshToken}}` (7 days, single use). Rate limited: 10 failed attempts per 15 minutes."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Me",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The logged-in user."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Token rotated', () => pm.expect(res.data.refreshToken).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('refreshToken')));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', res.data.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', res.data.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges the refresh token for a **new access token and a new refresh token** (rotation — each refresh token works once).\n\nBrowsers send the refresh cookie automatically and can post an empty body; API clients send `refreshToken` in the body. Call this when a request fails with `401` and `code: \"TOKEN_EXPIRED\"`, then retry the request.\n\nError codes: `REFRESH_TOKEN_MISSING`, `REFRESH_TOKEN_INVALID` (expired / logged out), `REFRESH_TOKEN_REUSED` (an old token was replayed — the whole session is revoked, log in again), `409 REFRESH_IN_PROGRESS` (another request just rotated it — retry).\n\nRunning this request twice in a row with the same old token demonstrates reuse detection."
          }
        },
